  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong> <a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://www.rbi.org.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Reserve Bank of India (RBI)</a></span> has released the admit card for the post of Officer Grade B (DR)- General, DEPR, DSIM.&nbsp;This recruitment was released for 60 posts. Applications for the RBI Officer Grade B Recruitment 2026 were accepted from April 29, 2026, to May 20, 2026. The online examination is going to be conducted on 13-14 June 2026. Candidates who had qualified this pre examination can download their RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card 2026 from the link given below.</span></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-2\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Reserve Bank of India (RBI)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card 2026</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">RBI Advt. No. : RBISB/BA/01/2026-27</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Application Start Date : <strong>29 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Last Date : <strong>20 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>20 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Correction Date : <strong>25-26 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase I Exam Date : <strong>13 June&nbsp;2026&nbsp;(DR General)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase I Exam Date :<strong>&nbsp;14 June 2026&nbsp;(DEPR/ DSIM)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase I Admit Card : <strong>05 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase II Exam Date : <strong>25&nbsp;July&nbsp;2026&nbsp;(DR General)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase II Exam Date :<strong>&nbsp;26 July&nbsp;2026&nbsp;(DEPR/ DSIM)</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General, EWS, OBC :<strong> Rs. 850/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST, PH :<strong> Rs. 100/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>RBI Officer Grade-B Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Age Limit As On 01 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum. Age :&nbsp;<strong>21 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum. Age :&nbsp;<strong>30 Years&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per RBI Officer Grade-B Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #0000ff; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>RBI Officer Grade-B 2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 60 Posts</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. of Posts</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – (General)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">40</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DEPR</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">10</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DSIM</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">10</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>RBI Officer Grade-B Recruitment 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.9905%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.0095%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.9905%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – (General)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.0095%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Graduation Level : </strong>Candidates must have completed their graduation in any discipline /Equivalent technical or professional qualification with a minimum 60% marks for General and 50% for SC / ST / PwBD applicants from any recognized University in India will be considered for this recruitment.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum 3 years duration from a recognized University/Institute.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post-Graduation Level : </strong>Candidates must have done their Post-Graduation / Equivalent technical qualification with a minimum of 55% marks (pass marks for SC / ST / PwBD applicants) in aggregate of all semesters/years from any recognized University in India will be considered for this recruitment.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum 2 years duration from a recognized University/Institute.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.9905%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DEPR</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.0095%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates must have completed their Master’s Degree in Economics / Econometrics / Quantitative Economics / Mathematical Economics / Integrated Economics Course / Finance with a minimum of 55% marks (50% in case of SC/ST/PWD) or an equivalent grade in aggregate of all semesters / years from any recognized University in India will be considered for this recruitment.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 28.9905%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Officers in Grade ‘B’ (DR) – DSIM</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 71.0095%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates must have completed their Master’s Degree in Economics / Econometrics / Quantitative Economics / Mathematical Economics / Integrated Economics Course / Finance with a minimum of 55% marks (50% in case of SC/ST/PWD) or an equivalent grade in aggregate of all semesters / years from any recognized University in India will be considered for this recruitment.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Download RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">In order to download their RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card candidates are required to go to the important link section provided below.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After getting the link candidates need to click it for downloading their RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates need to provide their following details-:</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Registration No. /Roll No.</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>DOB/Password</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Captcha Code(if specified)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After providing their details appropriately candidates will be able to check their RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates can also check their RBI Officer Grade B Admit Card from official site of the RBI.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>RBI Officer Grade-B Recruitment 2026 : Mode of Selection</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase-I Written Exam</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Phase-II Written Exam</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Personal Interview</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Document Verification</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Medical Examination</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\"><strong>Follow SarkariExam on Instagram</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"post-social-link\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"3\" data-align=\"center\"><strong></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"tex